  ('Bachelor of Electronics Engineering with Honours', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Infrastructure University Kuala Lumpur (IUKL)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4269, '4 years', '["Mar","Jun","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Electronics Engineering with Honours Program at Infrastructure University Kuala Lumpur (IUKL) University Malaysia focuses on providing essential knowledge and practical skills in electronics engineering. It covers topics such as circuit theory, electronic devices, digital electronics, microprocessors, and control system engineering. This program is suitable for those interested in mathematics, science, energy, and electronic gadgets. Graduates can work in various industries such as telecommunications, manufacturing, research, and healthcare. The program is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Council (EAC) and recognized internationally under the Washington Accord, offering global recognition and career opportunities.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

