  ('Bachelor of Landscape Architecture', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Infrastructure University Kuala Lumpur (IUKL)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 5693, '3 years', '["Mar","Jun","Nov"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Landscape Architecture Program at Infrastructure University Kuala Lumpur (IUKL) University Malaysia focuses on designing outdoor spaces and environments. It is suitable for individuals interested in design and with good drawing skills. The program includes design projects, site visits, and internships. Graduates can pursue careers as Landscape Architects in various sectors. The average salary for fresh graduates ranges from RM 2,000 to RM 3,000. The program emphasizes sustainable designs, construction technology, innovation, and management. A passion for landscapes is important for success in this field.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

