  ('Master of Quality Engineering and Management', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UniKL University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4347, '1.5 years', '["Jan","Jul","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Quality Engineering and Management (MQEM) program is a unique blend of academic learning and professional certification, designed to equip students with comprehensive skills in Quality Engineering (QE) and Management. Through a combination of rigorous coursework and certification from bodies like the Chartered Quality Institute and Lean Center of Excellence, students gain theoretical knowledge and practical expertise in Total Quality Management (TQM) and Lean Six Sigma methodologies. The program aims to produce graduates who can lead quality improvement initiatives and technopreneurial ventures, making them highly sought-after professionals in various industries. MQEM attracts both domestic and international participants, offering opportunities for career advancement and specialization in advanced manufacturing, inspection, and quality improvement methodologies. Ultimately, graduates emerge as competent QE professionals and quality managers ready to excel in today''s dynamic job market.

