  ('Bachelor of Accounting (Honours)', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Tunku Abdul Rahman University (UTAR)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 3443, '4 years', '["Oct","Feb","Jun"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Accounting (Honours) program at Tunku Abdul Rahman University (UTAR) focuses on the systematic processes of recording, categorizing, analyzing, reporting, and preparing financial statements in accordance with established rules and regulations governing financial reporting. Students in this program gain a comprehensive understanding of accounting principles, practices, and standards. They learn how to accurately record financial transactions, classify them into relevant categories, analyze financial data, and prepare financial statements such as income statements, balance sheets, and cash flow statements. The program emphasizes the importance of adhering to regulatory frameworks and ethical considerations in financial reporting. Graduates of the program are equipped with the knowledge and skills necessary to pursue careers in accounting, auditing, financial analysis, and financial management, where they play a vital role in ensuring accurate and reliable financial information for decision-making and compliance purposes.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

