  ('Bachelor of Science (Honours) Biotechnology', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Tunku Abdul Rahman University (UTAR)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4448, '3 years', '["Oct","Feb","Jun"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Science (Honours) in Biotechnology program at Tunku Abdul Rahman University (UTAR) focuses on the application of advancements made in the biological sciences, particularly in the field of genetics. Biotechnology plays a crucial role in enhancing food quality, quantity, and processing. It involves the manipulation of cells and proteins to produce chemicals, leading to innovative solutions in various industries. Moreover, biotechnology has significant implications in the field of health and medicine. Through genetic engineering, scientists have achieved remarkable breakthroughs, including the development of new medicines such as interferon for cancer patients, synthetic human growth hormone, synthetic insulin, and more. The program equips students with a comprehensive understanding of the principles and applications of biotechnology. They delve into subjects such as genetics, molecular biology, biochemistry, and bioprocessing. Students also gain practical laboratory skills and learn about ethical considerations in biotechnology. Graduates of the Bachelor of Science (Honours) Biotechnology program are well-prepared to contribute to the biotechnology industry. They can pursue careers in areas such as pharmaceuticals, agriculture, environmental sciences, and research institutions, where they can actively participate in advancing scientific knowledge and developing innovative solutions for the benefit of society.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

