  ('Bachelor of Science (Honours) Occupational Safety and Health with Environmental Health', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Tunku Abdul Rahman University (UTAR)' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 4362, '3.5 years', '["Oct","Feb","Jun"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Science (Honours) Occupational Safety and Health with Environmental Health program at Tunku Abdul Rahman University (UTAR) addresses the pressing global issues caused by climate change, pollution, and the depletion of natural resources, which have had adverse effects on human health and led to the rise of various diseases. This program recognizes the significance of environmental protection and the need for comprehensive legal frameworks to control hazardous substances, promote green technologies and materials, and develop effective waste treatment technologies. By studying this program, students gain a deep understanding of occupational safety and health principles, environmental risk assessment, pollution control, and sustainable practices. They also acquire practical skills in implementing safety measures, conducting environmental audits, and promoting health and safety in the workplace. Graduates of the Bachelor of Science (Honours) Occupational Safety and Health with Environmental Health program are well-prepared to pursue careers in various sectors, including industry, manufacturing, construction, healthcare, and government agencies. They play a vital role in ensuring workplace safety, protecting the environment, and promoting sustainable practices, thus contributing to the well-being of individuals, communities, and the planet as a whole.

