  ('Bachelor in Mechanical Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 12540, '4 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor in Mechanical Engineering (Hons) program at Nottingham University Malaysia offers a comprehensive curriculum that includes lectures, laboratory classes, workshops, and design classes. The courses focus on core engineering science and design skills to provide students with a strong foundation. In the Department of Mechanical, Materials, and Manufacturing Engineering, students gain theoretical knowledge and hands-on experience through practical work in labs and workshops. They also have the opportunity to apply their learning by conducting investigations and transforming designs into reality using Computer-Aided Design (CAD) software, Computer-Aided Engineering (CAE), and design projects.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

