  ('Bachelor in Mechatronic Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 12540, '4 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor in Mechatronic Engineering (Hons) program at Nottingham University Malaysia prepares students to work as professional mechatronic engineers. The program focuses on practical knowledge and skills in examining and programming mechatronic systems, including instrumentation, measurement, control of hydraulic and electrical systems, and robotics concepts. By specializing in mechatronic engineering, students explore new technologies in automation and robotics for tasks in hazardous environments and precise positioning, benefiting health, safety, society, and the economy.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

