  ('Bachelor of Pharmacy', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 13200, '4 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Pharmacy (Honours) program at Nottingham University Malaysia is a 4-year degree program offered at the Malaysia campus. The program consists of modules that contribute to specific credit requirements. The curriculum focuses on integration across therapeutic themes or disease states through "Drug, Medicine, and Patient" (DMP) modules. Each topic is examined from the perspectives of the drug, the medicine, and the patient. The emphasis on DMP modules is in Years 1 to 3, along with a research project module to develop research and data analysis skills. In Year 4, students engage in extended placements in industrial and community pharmacy settings.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Optional modules are health sciences related and support the pharmacist’s competencies development

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Traditional Pharmacy Career Paths. Pharmacist. ...\nResearch and Development (R&D) Research Scientist. ...\nRegulatory Affairs. Regulatory Affairs Specialist. ...\nQuality Control and Quality Assurance. ...\nAcademia and Teaching. ...\nEntrepreneurship. ...\nGovernment and Public Sector Jobs. ..."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'STPM

BBB, excluding Pengajian Am..

