  ('Biomedical Sciences MPhil - Molecular', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 16371, '1 year', '["Feb","Apr","Jun","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The MPhil and PhD biomedical programs have durations of 1-2 years and 3-4 years, respectively. Research is essential to the biomedical industry, with many of our academic staff at the forefront of scientific and healthcare advancements. The current research curriculum provides students with hands-on experience in their chosen fields and includes participation in regular research symposiums. These opportunities help students develop their research networks and hone their science outreach skills.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

With a diverse range of potential specializations, our Biomedical Sciences research degree is specifically designed to enhance your career options. A robust toolkit of research skills provides an excellent foundation for entering the biomedical or biotechnology industries, whether in research roles or clinical trials evaluation. This qualification enables graduates to work as medical scientific liaisons, assisting healthcare professionals in interpreting advanced research data. The University of Nottingham Malaysia has a strong track record of producing academics who work in institutions around the globe, training the next generation of biomedical scientists.

In the area of healthcare delivery systems, we extract innovative models and approaches from across sectors to alleviate health challenges in resource-limited low-income countries.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["With a diverse range of potential specializations, our Biomedical Sciences research degree is specifically designed to enhance your career options. A robust toolkit of research skills provides an excellent foundation for entering the biomedical or biotechnology industries, whether in research roles or clinical trials evaluation. This qualification enables graduates to work as medical scientific liaisons, assisting healthcare professionals in interpreting advanced research data. The University of Nottingham Malaysia has a strong track record of producing academics who work in institutions around the globe, training the next generation of biomedical scientists."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'An upper second class honours degree (or international equivalent) in biomedical sciences, pharmacology, pharmacy or a related scientific discipline. Non-UK qualifications will be assessed against this standard.
If deemed necessary, applicants may also be required to attend an interview.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
