  ('Biosciences research programmes MPhil -Non-molecular', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 12899, '1 year', '["Feb","Apr","Jun","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'We provide high-quality doctoral training for postgraduate students interested in pursuing an MPhil, MRes, or PhD. As a research student, you will collaborate with a supervisor who will guide you in your research and thesis design.

The MPhil is a shorter research degree that involves a project over one to two years, while the PhD consists of an independent, in-depth research project that allows you to develop additional skills through various training programs offered by the School. Both the MPhil and PhD are assessed through a research thesis. The MRes is typically a one-year program that combines taught modules with a research project.

You will have regular meetings with your supervisor and an annual review of your research progress. Current research areas of interest within the School include the development of climate-resilient crops, exploration of underutilized crops to enhance food and nutritional security, reduction of food waste, and more.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

The comprehensive scientific training provided by the School’s postgraduate research programs opens up a variety of career options for graduates. As a world-class educational institution, students acquire valuable transferable skills applicable in both industry and further education.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["The comprehensive scientific training provided by the School’s postgraduate research programs opens up a variety of career options for graduates. As a world-class educational institution, students acquire valuable transferable skills applicable in both industry and further education.\n\nCareer opportunities include roles such as scientific officers and managers, product development executives, academic educators, agricultural and environmental consultants, food and nutrition advisors, and scientific writers. Additional prospects within industry may include positions as forensic biologists, professionals in pharmaceutical development, business managers, food manufacturing specialists, or even successful bio-entrepreneurs."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'An upper second class honours degree (or international equivalent) in an agricultural, biological or other relevant science disciplines. Non-UK qualifications will be assessed against this standard.
If deemed necessary, applicants may also be required to attend an interview.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
