  ('BSc in Psychology', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 10648, '3 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Psychology is the scientific study of behavior and mental processes in humans and other species, focusing on individuals, groups, organizations, and societies. It has a wide-ranging application, addressing issues relevant to both individuals and communities, as well as clinical and non-clinical (typical) populations.

The field of psychology encompasses various inquiries, such as how a child with minimal knowledge of the world matures into a skilled and knowledgeable adult. It also examines contemporary societal trends, including the impact of social media on individuals and communities, and how vulnerable or clinical populations, such as those with autism, navigate a changing world. Psychology is a rigorous science, and our students develop strong analytical thinking, statistical skills, and the ability to evaluate scientific evidence. They learn to comprehend, conduct, and present scientific research, while also becoming effective communicators and proficient scientific writers.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Social Worker. \nCareer Counselor. \nPsychiatric Technician. \nHealth Educator. \nHuman Resource Specialist. \nCommunity Service Manager. \nSocial and Human Service Assistant"]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'STPM

