  ('BSc in Psychology and Cognitive Neuroscience', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 10648, '3 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Psychology is the scientific study of behavior and mental processes in humans and other species, focusing on individuals, groups, organizations, and societies. Cognitive Neuroscience specifically examines the brain and its mechanisms that influence these behaviors and mental processes. This program is more concentrated on concepts and research methods in Cognitive Neuroscience compared to the BSc Psychology program, requiring students to select 40 credits of cognitive neuroscience-related modules in their final year. However, both programs share significant overlap and aim to provide a solid foundation in Psychology. The field has broad applications in relation to both individuals and communities, as well as clinical and non-clinical (typical) populations.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

