  ('Developmental Disorders MSc', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 12518, '1 year', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Science (MSc) in Developmental Disorders, which aligns with the parallel program at the UK campus, provides advanced theoretical knowledge of the psychological aspects of neurodevelopmental, clinical, and behavioral conditions that emerge during childhood and impact various areas of a child''s life. Examples of developmental disorders include Autism, Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD), Tic Disorders, and Learning Disorders (such as dyslexia and dysgraphia).

