  ('Master of Business Administration MBA', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 15040, '1 year', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Our MBA program focuses on general financial and corporate management. It enhances the value of your first degree by fostering an integrated and critically aware understanding of management and organizations within an international context.

This program will broaden your career prospects and earning potential while enhancing your CV. An MBA will elevate your employability, making you an attractive candidate for prestigious employers seeking your skill set.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

The Nottingham MBA is designed for individuals aiming to unlock their potential to manage and lead in today’s dynamic and complex organizational environment. This qualification is highly regarded in both the public and private sectors, making it valuable for middle and senior-level managers as well as entrepreneurs. The program will enhance your management skills for senior roles, improve your career prospects, and cultivate your leadership capabilities.

You must complete a total of 12 taught modules (8 core modules and 4 elective modules) and a Management Project.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["The Nottingham MBA is designed for individuals aiming to unlock their potential to manage and lead in today’s dynamic and complex organizational environment. This qualification is highly regarded in both the public and private sectors, making it valuable for middle and senior-level managers as well as entrepreneurs. The program will enhance your management skills for senior roles, improve your career prospects, and cultivate your leadership capabilities."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A relevant second class honours degree (or international equivalent) or a relevant professional qualification deemed equivalent to a first degree with honours, plus at least three or more years of full-time management or leadership work experience, normally gained since graduating from the first degree. Non-UK qualifications will be assessed against this standard.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Mathematical Sciences MPhil', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 11410, '1 year', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Join the School of Mathematical Sciences to engage in projects that explore both fundamental and applied mathematical sciences, aimed at solving a diverse array of real-world problems. Projects encompass the following areas:

We are looking for enthusiastic research students who are keen to shape the future of mathematical sciences and make a positive impact on the world. Our research projects span a wide range, from developing innovative mathematical models to applying mathematical sciences in the creation of sustainable materials and advancements in healthcare. Join us and contribute to making a difference through your passion for research.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

A postgraduate qualification in Mathematics or Statistics can open the door to various roles, including academic positions, data scientist, policy analyst, or economist in government organizations and research institutes. Graduates may also find opportunities in banks and investment firms, health research institutes, or as management consultants in fields such as finance, insurance, IT, engineering, market research, and management consulting.

Throughout your PhD you will focus on learning what information is already published and identifying gaps in knowledge. You will start to formulate your own research questions and develop skills to become a professional researcher.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["A postgraduate qualification in Mathematics or Statistics can open the door to various roles, including academic positions, data scientist, policy analyst, or economist in government organizations and research institutes. Graduates may also find opportunities in banks and investment firms, health research institutes, or as management consultants in fields such as finance, insurance, IT, engineering, market research, and management consulting."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'An upper second class honours degree (or international equivalent) in mathematics or a closely related discipline with substantial mathematical content. Non-UK qualifications will be assessed against this standard.
If deemed necessary, applicants may also be required to attend an interview.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
