  ('Social and Behavioural Science (Economics) PhD', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'PhD', 10098, '3 years', '["Sep"]'::jsonb, 'Our PhD Economics program provides high-quality doctoral training in research skills while offering knowledge in specialized fields. Current research areas at the School of Economics include behavioral economics, development economics, experimental economics, international economics, microeconomics, and macroeconomics. Throughout the program, our postgraduate students will acquire a strong foundation in all areas of economics, as well as the tools, techniques, and literature essential for writing a PhD dissertation.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

A PhD in Economics equips you with invaluable skills and strong career credentials. You can apply your expertise in roles such as researchers, academics, economists, and economic consultants. These positions often highly value the skills developed through a postgraduate qualification.

In broader contexts, additional career options related to economics include financial risk analysts, investment analysts, and quantitative analysts. You could work in banks, hedge funds, and investment banks that utilize models and analyses to evaluate financial risks. Furthermore, some management consultancies and larger financial firms employ economic consultants to help organizations solve problems and enhance business performance.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["A PhD in Economics equips you with invaluable skills and strong career credentials. You can apply your expertise in roles such as researchers, academics, economists, and economic consultants. These positions often highly value the skills developed through a postgraduate qualification.\n\nIn broader contexts, additional career options related to economics include financial risk analysts, investment analysts, and quantitative analysts. You could work in banks, hedge funds, and investment banks that utilize models and analyses to evaluate financial risks. Furthermore, some management consultancies and larger financial firms employ economic consultants to help organizations solve problems and enhance business performance."]'::jsonb, 'Free', 'A Master of Science in Economics with a merit grade (or international equivalent). Non-UK qualifications will be assessed against this standard.
If deemed necessary, applicants may also be required to attend an interview.

