  ('Social and Behavioural Science (Politics, history development and international relations) PhD', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'Nottingham University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'PhD', 10098, '3 years', '["Feb","Apr","Jun","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'We provide high-quality doctoral training for postgraduate students aiming to pursue a PhD. As a research student, you will collaborate with a supervisor who will guide you in your research and thesis design. While principal supervisors are typically members of our school, secondary supervisors may be selected from other schools within the faculty, as well as from the School of Politics and International Relations in the UK or the Division of International Studies in Ningbo, China.

For other qualifications and certificates please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

The University’s Career Advisory Services (CAS) support students in acquiring essential skills and accessing career opportunities through strong relationships with various employers and industries. The CAS offers vital resources and guidance for making informed career choices, providing numerous opportunities to develop the skills necessary for planning and managing your future.

Our Careers Advisory Service will work with you to enhance and maximize your employability skills, while also providing crucial resources and assistance with job and course applications. They will facilitate the search for suitable work experience placements and connect you with a wide array of prospective employers and training opportunities.

