  ('Bachelor of Psychology', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'MONASH University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Bachelor', 10982, '3 years', '["Feb","Jul","Oct"]'::jsonb, 'The Bachelor of Psychology Program at MONASH University Malaysia provides a strong foundation in psychological theories and research. It prepares students for careers in clinical psychology, management, research, teaching, human resources, community services, and counseling health services. The program explores the biopsychosocial factors influencing human behavior and emphasizes evidence-based approaches and scientific methodology. It offers specialization options in mental health and wellbeing or applied psychology. The degree is accredited by the Australian Psychology Accreditation Council (APAC), enabling further study in psychology in Australia.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

These studies will address core areas of psychology, including the theoretical and empirical basis of our current understanding of human psychology, brain function and evidence-based approaches to psychological intervention. Building a strong foundation in your understanding of psychology will enable you to appreciate the major challenges in psychology today and in the future.

