  ('Master of Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4400, '1.5 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Engineering (Computer and Microelectronic Systems) program at Universiti Teknologi Malaysia is designed to provide students with advanced knowledge and skills in the fields of computer engineering, IC microchip design, microelectronics systems, and advanced electronics in new generation technologies. The program aims to address the challenges faced by semiconductor-based companies in producing smaller, higher performance, and cost-effective microchips that meet the growing demand for digital devices. It offers a comprehensive curriculum that covers both theoretical concepts and practical applications, allowing engineers to enhance their knowledge and skills while complementing their industrial expertise. The program is developed in close collaboration with industry partners, such as Intel, ensuring that it meets the technical needs for upskilling and advancing the knowledge of engineers. The program offers both full-time and part-time options, with full-time classes conducted at the main campus in Johor Bahru and part-time classes held at the INTEL campus in Penang. The program can be completed within two years, consisting of four regular semesters and one short semester. Classes for the part-time program are scheduled on Saturdays and Sundays at the study center. The program fees are affordable and competitive, making it accessible to a wide range of students.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

Thank you  for submitting your form to us. We will contact you as soon as possible to assist you on your university journey.', '[]'::jsonb, '{"min_gpa":"2.0","ielts":"5.5"}'::jsonb, '["Specialist in field"]'::jsonb, 'Fees Applies', 'Bachelor''s Degree: Candidates should possess a good honors bachelor''s degree in Civil Engineering from Universiti Teknologi Malaysia or an equivalent qualification. The degree should have a Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) of 2.5 and above. The bachelor''s degree should provide a solid foundation in civil engineering principles and relevant coursework.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.'),
  ('Master of Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4400, '1.5 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Engineering (Construction Management) at UTM University Malaysia is designed for professionals seeking to advance their expertise in the construction industry. The program covers essential areas such as project management, construction technology, and sustainable practices.

Students will engage in advanced coursework and research that focuses on the complexities of managing construction projects effectively. The curriculum emphasizes both theoretical knowledge and practical skills, enabling graduates to tackle real-world challenges in construction management.

Key components of the program include specialized subjects in project planning, risk management, contract administration, and construction law. Students will also have opportunities for hands-on learning and collaboration with industry professionals.

This master''s program is ideal for engineers, project managers, and other professionals looking to enhance their competencies and career prospects in the construction sector.

