  ('Master of Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4400, '1.5 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Engineering (Structure) programme at Universiti Teknologi Malaysia is designed to provide students with the knowledge and skills necessary to address complex problems in civil engineering structures. Through advanced training in structural analysis and design, students gain expertise in various areas, including advanced structural analysis, the finite element method, reinforced and precast concrete, steel, cold-formed and composite structures, structural dynamics, wind and earthquake engineering, tall buildings, bridges, and the design and safety of temporary structures. The programme also offers the opportunity for students to engage in research or design projects, allowing them to enhance their practical skills and expertise in the field.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

