  ('Master of Engineering (Transportation)', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4400, '1.5 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Engineering (Transportation) program at Universiti Teknologi Malaysia is available in full-time mode and follows a 3-Semester Academic Session structure. Each semester comprises various courses that are delivered and evaluated. Assessment methods include final examinations, coursework throughout the semester, and a Master Project. To successfully graduate from the program, students must accumulate a minimum of 46 credit hours with a minimum Cumulative Point Average (CPA) of 3.0.Upon completion of the program, graduates possess profound and relevant knowledge applicable to professional practices, benefiting both national and international communities. They are equipped to apply their expertise and skills in the planning, analysis, design, and supervision of projects within the field of civil engineering. Furthermore, graduates are capable of formulating hypotheses, designing and conducting scientific experiments or research to solve problems and provide explanations for observed phenomena.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

