  ('Master of Philosophy in Bioprocess Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 3124, '2 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Philosophy programme in the field of Bioprocess Engineering (MKKB) at Universiti Teknologi Malaysia (UTM) is offered on a full-time basis, with a study duration ranging from one (1) year to a maximum of four (4) years. The research program assessment is conducted through progress reports, supervisor''s evaluations, research proposals, and a viva voce examination. The programme aims to apply advanced knowledge in bioprocess engineering and develop students'' abilities to design and manage scientific research using acceptable methodologies, while employing effective thinking skills. Critical analysis and evaluation of problems in related areas are emphasized, utilizing appropriate tools and techniques. Effective communication of technical findings, both in written and oral forms, is expected. The programme promotes intellectual honesty and integrity in performing scientific work and encourages students to identify and apply available information and research evidence within the relevant context.

