  ('Master of Philosophy in Electrical Engineering', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 3124, '2 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Philosophy (M.Phil.) program at Universiti Teknologi Malaysia, offered at FKE (Faculty of Electrical Engineering), is a research-based degree program designed for individuals with a Bachelor''s degree in Electrical Engineering or a related field who wish to expand and enhance their knowledge. This program is multidisciplinary in nature and aims to help candidates develop high-level analytical and presentation skills while integrating academic and professional considerations. Successful completion of the program indicates that candidates have undergone rigorous research training. The M.Phil. thesis is expected to make a valuable contribution to the existing body of knowledge in the field. The degree is awarded based on a comprehensive oral examination (viva voce) of the candidate''s thesis upon completion of their studies. Prospective graduate students should adequately prepare themselves in the fundamental subject matter necessary for advanced work and other relevant areas of learning to conduct high-quality research and successfully complete the program.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., Other qualifications equivalent to a Bachelor’s degree , etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

