  ('Master of Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 3691, '1.5 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Science in Sustainable Infrastructure (MSSI) program at Universiti Teknologi Malaysia is designed to provide comprehensive knowledge and opportunities for graduates and professionals with backgrounds in engineering, science, and technology to enhance their understanding of sustainable infrastructure. This program focuses on practical applications and industry-driven approaches, allowing participants to directly contribute value to their employers and the industry as a whole. Experienced industrial speakers deliver lectures throughout the modules, ensuring that participants gain insights from real-world expertise in sustainable infrastructure. The program requires a total of 46 credits for graduation, which includes 12 modules of 3 credits each and a 10-credit master project. The duration of study is 1.5 years for full-time students and 2 years for part-time students. The MSSI program aims to prepare professionals in engineering, science, and technology-based organizations for senior executive positions or senior engineering management roles, fostering a mindset of lifelong learning and continuous professional development.

For other qualifications and certificates (e.g., UEC, Foundation, STAM, etc..) please contact our educational consultants or submit your application for Admission assessment.

