  ('Master of Science', (SELECT id FROM public.universities WHERE name = 'UTM University Malaysia' LIMIT 1), 'Master', 4400, '1.5 years', '["Feb","Sep"]'::jsonb, 'The Master of Science in Sustainable Urban Design program at Universiti Teknologi Malaysia stands as the sole industry-oriented coursework-based program in Malaysia that specifically tackles prevalent local and global sustainability challenges in the built environment. This interdisciplinary program amalgamates the realms of architecture, urban planning, environmental planning, landscape architecture, and environmental engineering. By fostering collaboration with allied professionals and partnering with local and international universities, the Master of Science in Sustainable Urban Design program integrates various aspects of sustainable development and urban design. To provide students with a broader perspective on global sustainability concerns, an obligatory overseas study trip is included as a vital component of the program. Through this comprehensive approach, students are equipped with the knowledge and skills to address the complex issues of sustainable urban design, contributing to the creation of environmentally conscious and socially responsible built environments.

